# Example R2DT_TEMPLATE lines for a VADR model info (.minfo) file.
#
# Add lines like these to the relevant MODEL's .minfo file (or to a sidecar
# .minfo passed to v-annotate.pl with --mdir) to enable R2DT secondary
# structure figure drawing with 'v-annotate.pl --draw_r2dt'.
#
# Documentation:
#   documentation/r2dt-drawing.md    (using --draw_r2dt)
#   documentation/r2dt-templates.md  (building and installing a template)
#
# WARNING: a .minfo file containing R2DT_TEMPLATE lines cannot be parsed by
# VADR 1.7 or earlier. Such a version rejects the whole model package, not
# just the drawing step. R2DT_TEMPLATE is first accepted by VADR 1.7.1.
#
# Syntax:
#   R2DT_TEMPLATE name=<r2dt_template_name> model=<vadr_model_name> ranges=<start>..<end>[,<start>..<end>]*
#
#   name    R2DT template name; a directory of that name must exist at
#           $R2DT_DIR/data/local_data/<name>/
#   model   VADR model name; must match a MODEL line's name in this .minfo
#   ranges  comma-separated list of inclusive, 1-indexed model (RF) position
#           ranges in the VADR model's own coordinate frame
#
# The three fields may appear in any order. All three are required.
#
# Rules for ranges, all enforced when the file is parsed, all fatal if broken:
#   - each range is <start>..<end> with start >= 1 and end >= start
#   - end must not exceed the model's consensus length (the MODEL line's
#     length: value)
#   - ranges on one line must be in ASCENDING order and must NOT OVERLAP
#
# The residues a sequence has at these positions are concatenated in the order
# the ranges are given, gaps are stripped, and the result is what R2DT draws.
# So the template's own consensus must be that same concatenation, in that
# same order, and the ranges must sum to the template's consensus length.
#
# Choosing the ranges is choosing the template's coverage: a sequence with no
# residues at these positions gets no diagram, with a warning rather than an
# error. See documentation/r2dt-drawing.md.
#
# One line per (model, template) pair. A model may have any number of
# templates; one is the common case.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# General form (substitute your own names and ranges):
#
# R2DT_TEMPLATE name=<template_name> model=<model_name> ranges=<start>..<end>
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Filled-in EXAMPLE ONLY, from a Zika virus model with two templates. Both
# templates cover a block at each end of the genome, because that is where
# this particular genome's structured elements are; that shape is a property
# of the genome, not of the mechanism. A model with one contiguous structured
# region would declare a single range.

R2DT_TEMPLATE name=zika-linear   model=MG807646 ranges=1..210,10380..10807
R2DT_TEMPLATE name=zika-circular model=MG807646 ranges=1..190,10666..10807
